data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Let $a = \\alpha + k$ and $b = \\beta + n - k$. The interior mode of $\\mathrm{Beta}(a,b)$ is $(a-1)/(a+b-2)$, which is\nvalid only when $a > 1$ and $b > 1$. Otherwise the peak is on the boundary: 0 when $a \\le 1$, and 1 when $b \\le 1$.\nValidate first: whole numbers, $n \\ge 1$, $0 \\le k \\le n$, and a finite positive prior."},"hints_note":null}

